>
>(I'm just wondering if there's anything to be gained by purchasing a 
>ZLXp-E3 rather than a ZLXp-E2.)

Our X server for the TGA cards doesn't make use of the Z buffer.
I don't think that XF86 does either, and IIRC a Z buffer only really
helps 3D apps---a rare commodity in the Open Source world (other
than xlockmore.)

